                <pb facs="0512" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v08/pg480"/>

                <head>132. Memorandum From the JCS Chairman’s Special Assistant (Goodpaster) to the
                    Assistant Secretary of Defense for International Security Affairs (Nitze)<anchor
                        n="0" xml:id="d132-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1963-04-20">April 20,
                    1963</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Major Military Issues in Basic National Security Policy</item>
                </list>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Attached is the document that I believe should be distributed for the
                        discussions between the Secretary and the Joint Chiefs of Staff on basic
                        national security policy. The document consists of three parts: <list>
                            <label>a.</label>
                            <item>A brief covering memorandum explaining the procedures used in
                                developing the material.</item>
                            <pb facs="0513" n="481" xml:id="pg481"/>
                            <label>b.</label>
                            <item>A summary of the six major issues.</item>
                            <label>c.</label>
                            <item>A three-column (State, JCS, OSD/ISA) tabulation of the issues as
                                extracted from the appropriate draft BNSP documents.<anchor n="1"
                                    xml:id="d132-f2"/></item>
                        </list></item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>With your concurrence I will have the document circulated to the Secretary
                        of Defense and the Joint Chiefs of Staff.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">A. J. Goodpaster</hi></signed><anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d132-f3"/><lb/>Major General, USA</closer>



                <xi:include href="d132-a1.xml" xpointer="d132-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d132-a2.xml" xpointer="d132-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
